# Same name 'env' appears at two different scopes.
# The outer intermediate binding 'env' is referenced by 'result'.
# 'result' is the final expression — so 'env' is transitively live.
# T-2071: BindingId (def_span + name) prevents the outer 'env' from being
# falsely flagged as lost when an inner dict also binds 'env'.
[call [fn [let x]
  [env: x]
  [result: [if true env "fallback"]]
  result]
"hello"]
=== out
String("hello")
